  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="896a-9bd6-a856-ed99" name="Persians and Medes (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #5 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list covers the rise of the Persian empire from the defeat of Babylon to the abandonment of traditional Persian infantry tactics and their wholesale replacement with Greek methods and mercenaries. After its initial successes the army became swollen with large contingents of subject peoples. The list can be used to construct the early army of Cyrus, or the army that faced the Greeks in Asia Minor and the invasions of Greece itself. Note: Some troops in this list are equipped with Spara, a very large cane wicker shield that was propped up in front of the unit for protection. Spara count as large shields and give the unit the Shieldwall rule as long as at least half the front rank is equipped with them. A fleeing unit abandons its Spara for the rest of the game. Note: Where troops in this army use the Combined Formation rule, all shooting casualties are taken from the ranks of archers. Allies And Mercenaries: A Cyrus period army may use camel mounted archers (see the allies’ section of the Lydian list). A Xerxes period army may use up to two units of mercenary hoplites from the Greek list, and may use up to two scythed chariots from the Later Persian list. Note that while the points for these chariots come from the allies and mercenaries’ section, they are not Unreliable.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Persians and Medes - Army of Cyrus]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Light Troops: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: up to 50% Infantry: At least 25% Light Troops: up to 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%
[Persians and Medes - Army of Xerxes]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Light Troops: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 25% Cavalry: up to 25% Infantry: At least 25% Light Troops: up to 25% Allies &amp; Mercenaries: up to 25%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
